A feed takes any delay, past WATCHDOG_US_MAX too;
the watchdog lies no further ahead than the longest delay a feed may name.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the watchdog is set further than the longest delay
Witness: fuzz watchdog-halts

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ static int op_clock(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, uint32_t op, uint32_t *arg)
     }
     case OP_CLOCK_WATCHDOG: {
         uint32_t us = arg[1];
-        if (us == 0 || us > WATCHDOG_US_MAX) {
+        if (us == 0) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         sched_watchdog(delay_deadline(us));
